# Bentonville Royale: optional local settings. Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in.
#
# Optional "Real-world 3D view (Google)" (Settings menu, off by default).
# Streams Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles around Bentonville; purely visual.
#
# 1. Google Cloud console: create/select a project and enable billing on it.
# 2. APIs & Services > Library: enable "Map Tiles API".
# 3. APIs & Services > Credentials: create an API key, then restrict it:
#      - Application restrictions: Websites (HTTP referrers) -> http://localhost:5173/*
#      - API restrictions: Map Tiles API only
# 4. Put the key below in .env.local and restart `npm run dev`.
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the client bundle: a key used in a deployed
# build is visible to anyone. Leave it unset for deploys (the toggle is then disabled
# and nothing is requested from Google), or use a separate, referrer-restricted key.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Multiplayer / parties / accounts server (Cloudflare Workers + Durable Objects, see
# wrangler.toml). Local dev: `npm run party:dev` serves localhost:1999, the default.
# Production: `npx wrangler login`, `npm run party:deploy`, then set this in Vercel to the
# printed host (no https://), e.g. bentonville-royale.<subdomain>.workers.dev
VITE_PARTYKIT_HOST=
